LEHU descends from FastCarPlay, a C++ CarPlay and Android Auto receiver:
  https://github.com/niellun/FastCarPlay  (Niellun and contributors, GPL-3.0)
  https://github.com/mbt28/FastCarPlay    (the F1C200s port, GPL-3.0)
Its designs for the protocols, the audio mixer, the video path and the
screens were carried over into Rust.

Session handling, device arbitration and several protocol behaviours
follow LIVI, a Rust CarPlay and Android Auto host:
  https://github.com/f-io/LIVI  (GPL-3.0)

vendor/fontique is fontique 0.11.1 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT, the Linebender
project) with a three-line change taken from LIVI for targets without
64-bit atomics. vendor/parley is parley 0.11.1 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT, the
Linebender project) with its dictionary segmenters left out to spare 3 MB
of tables. The screens embed Open Sans Regular (Apache-2.0).

crates/lehu-video/csrc/decoder.c (the ffmpeg v4l2-request decoder handing
out dma-bufs) follows LIVI's decoder.c, itself ported from FastCarPlay's
V4l2DrmDecoder; both GPL-3.0.

crates/lehu-aa speaks the Android Auto (GAL) protocol as reverse engineered
by aasdk (f1x.studio, GPL-3.0) and carried on by LIVI: the message ids,
the protobuf field numbers of the messages the head unit uses, and the
head-unit client certificate aasdk published, which phones accept, come
from there through FastCarPlay's native backend.

Now playing and route guidance take their message ids, parameter ids,
the route guidance display component and the manoeuvre tables from LIVI:
its iAP2 messages (crates/lehu-cp/src/media.rs) and its Android Auto
media playback and navigation status definitions
(crates/lehu-aa/src/status.rs), GPL-3.0.

The album art over iAP2 file transfer (crates/lehu-cp/src/file.rs) takes
the artwork's transfer id attribute, the file transfer session and its
control codes from LIVI's iAP2 messages and file transfer receiver, and
the Android Auto album art field from its media metadata definition,
GPL-3.0.

CarPlay Ultra (crates/lehu-cp/src/mfi4.rs with mfi4/, opack.rs,
vehicle.rs, ui_sync.rs and ultra.rs) follows LIVI's: the MFi 4 mutual
authentication (its message and parameter ids, the SIGMA-I key
derivation and channels, the compressed certificate layout and the DER
rebuilt from it, the tunneled pair-setup and the pair-verify binding),
the OPACK codec, the vehicle state protocol and its route sharing
accessory, the UI sync messages, the display panel carrying the plug-in,
the start and identification parameters for mutual authentication and
the theme, and the theme catalog query in scripts/ultra-theme.py,
GPL-3.0. The key material and certificate tests use values computed
with LIVI's code.
